sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ
    participant C as Consumer (any of the four)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL (its schema)
    MQ->>C: deliver message (MessageId m)
    C->>PG: one transaction: business change + Inbox row m
    PG-->>C: commit
    Note over C: process killed before the ack
    Note over MQ: unacked message returns to the queue
    MQ->>C: redeliver message m (after restart)
    C->>PG: Inbox: m already processed? (yes)
    C-->>MQ: ack as no-op
    Note over PG: one effect, timestamps unchanged
